\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Transfer operators of the Gaussian chain}
\date{2026-11-01}

\p{A nearest-neighbor Gaussian energy factors into kernels between
successive time slices. Composing those kernels gives a transfer
operator; closing the chain gives its trace. For a single real field
per slice, Hermite functions diagonalize the operator exactly.
The leading eigenvalue fixes the normalization needed before its
logarithm becomes a nonnegative Hamiltonian.}

\p{The construction uses positive weight and mass, Lebesgue measure
on each field coordinate and a unit time step. It supplies the
operator structure that [reflection positivity alone](fdip-007Q)
does not determine. The [cycle determinant](fdip-006G) and
[periodic covariance](fdip-0057) give independent finite-dimensional
checks of its partition function and field correlations.}

\transclude{fdip-007T}
